      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are absolutely right; these phrases function as linguistic euphemisms that psychologically numb audiences by sanitizing complex realities into routine bureaucratic speak. In pragmatics, this phenomenon, often linked to \"bureaucratic avoidance,\" deliberately creates emotional distance to prevent scrutiny of the underlying issues. While not always formally codified, these tropes rely on well-documented psychological effects where vague, time-bound language induces compliance and reduces cognitive resistance.",
